      "text": "**Meeting Summary – OpenClaw Q2 Planning (2026‑04‑01)**  \n\nThe session focused on aligning the OpenClaw product roadmap, budget, and resource constraints for Q2.  \n- **Product**: The core Q2 deliverable is the “M1” milestone, an externally demo‑ready release due May 15. It will include workspace rule improvements, a smoother handoff experience, and a stabilized evaluation pipeline. Two checkpoints were set: all P0 defects cleared by April 30, and the demo‑ready build shipped by May 15. If the schedule slips, the core path will be protected and any non‑core features—such as the optional multimodal plugin pack—will be deferred to Q3.  \n- **Engineering**: The main risk is regressions between the gateway and local embedded modes. Plans include adding smoke tests and nightly batches. Staffing is limited to two backend and one frontend full‑time engineers; Operations will provide a batch of declassified sample tasks to support regression testing. A hiring freeze could force the removal of the multimodal plugin pack from M1.  \n- **Finance**: The R&D budget is locked at Q1 levels; marketing and travel expenses require separate approvals.  \n- **Operations**: Will deliver 20 user task descriptions within two weeks and draft FAQ updates for the help center.  \n\n**Key action items**  \n1. Zhang Min – refresh and broadcast the roadmap to all hands by Friday.  \n2. Li – publish the risk list and test‑case priorities by next Wednesday.  \n3. Chen – deliver the sample task pack by April 18.  \n\n**Open issue** – Whether the hiring freeze will continue through Q2 is pending HR next week; if it does, Product must trim the M1 scope.  \n\nThe meeting adjourned with a clear focus on meeting the April 30 P0 defect deadline and the May 15 demo milestone while monitoring budget and staffing constraints.",
      "mediaUrl": null
    }
