entation claims all nodes are in `us-east-1`, but actual data contradicts this.\n\n## 3. Required Artifacts\nAfter completing the task, you must produce:\n- `/workspace/out/audit_report.csv`: Audit report. Must contain six column headers: `Source_A`, `Source_B`, `Config_Key`, `Value_A`, `Value_B`, `Issue_Type`. Each row records one inconsistency. `Issue_Type` can be: `config_mismatch`, `env_override_mismatch`, `hardware_mismatch`, `region_mismatch`.\n  - For config conflicts: `Source_A=\"db_global\"`, `Source_B=\"deployment_guide\"`\n  - For environment override conflicts: Production environment: `Source_A=\"db_global\"`, `Source_B=\"configmap_production\"`; Staging environment: `Source_A=\"db_staging\"`, `Source_B=\"configmap_staging\"`. Note: In this task, production has a `session_timeout_min` mismatch (db_global=15, configmap_production=30); staging environment has all configurations consistent, **do not produce any `env_override_mismatch` for staging**.\n  - For hardware conflicts: `Source_A=\"db_cluster_nodes\"` or `\"node_inventory\"`, `Source_B=\"deployment_guide\"`, `Config_Key` format `node_id.hardware_field` (e.g., `web-01.cpu_cores`).\n  - For region conflicts: same, `Config_Key` format `node_id.region`.\n- `/workspace/out/progress.md`: Brief record of how you extracted and compared the data.\n\n## 4. Constraints\n- **No hallucination**: Do not fabricate any report content; all data must come from the provided files.\n- **Precise extraction**: Do not modify the original documentation or SQL files; your only task is to output a comparison report.\n- **Multi‑source cross‑reference**: When multiple sources (DB and JSON) describe the same node, they are considered consistent ground‑truth sources; only compare them against the documentation.\n- **Multi‑source consistency**: If `backup.sql`'s `cluster_nodes` table and `node_inventory.json` describe the same node, they are considered consistent; if they differ, `backup.sql` takes precedence – **do not report such internal inconsistencies as contradictions**.\n- **Zero false positives**: Only report true inconsistencies. If a configuration item is consistent across all sources (e.g., some staging configurations), **do not report it as a contradiction**.\n\nBenchmark output contract: Write prose deliverables in English. Preserve the specified filenames, commands, identifiers, JSON keys, enum values, headings, and exact output strings.\n",
